{
	title: 'Solid on the newest 2.0 release',
	spec: "The web client uses the newest SolidJS 2.0 release (2.0.0-rc.11 or later, with its matching compiler), not a pin to an old rc. Before bumping, the event bug that made rc.9 unusable is checked again with a test that fails if events silently stop (the one 1b's notes describe); if it still breaks, the pin stays with a note naming the broken version (questions.md 86).",
	status: 'done',
	needs: [],
	foldInto: ['1b'],
	notes: [
		'2026-09-29: Tried SolidJS 2.0.0-rc.11 (@solidjs/web and @solidjs/signals rc.11) with newest published @dom-expressions/compiler 0.50.0-next.44. Browser CDP regression passed rc.8 and failed rc.11: onInput does not enable Send (delegated event silently missing). Keep rc.8 pinned until the compiler emits the delegated-event key rc.11 expects; the CDP test checks onInput and onClick in a real browser.'
	]
}
